/*! \page sdk_tools SDK and Host Tools

Markdown companion: \c docs/tools.md.

\section sdk_tools_scaffold Scaffold

\c tools/scaffold_class_a_cuda.py generates an external Class-A CUDA project
(\c ce, \c equalizer, or \c receiver) that depends only on installed
\c OCUDUDAppSDK and refuses to overwrite an existing path.

\section sdk_tools_certify Certifier

\c certify_class_a_cuda loads a final DSO through the public ABI, runs the full
null-configuration lifecycle, exercises concurrent workers and streams, and
checks the declared shape/QAM/DM-RS matrix with poisoned-buffer canaries.
Optional model arguments exercise receiver model generations.

\section sdk_tools_model Model helper

\c make_receiver_cuda_model emits the reference receiver model artifact for
demos only. Product packages must supply their own exporter.

\section sdk_tools_python_example Python Class-C example

\c examples/class_c_e3_python demonstrates Class-C out-of-process sensing with
PyTorch (supervised process packages + optional portable E3). Research only;
not Class-A/B or in-process MODULEs. See \c examples/class_c_e3_python/README.md
and \c docs/tools.md.

\section sdk_tools_host Host tools

Installed with OCUDU: \c ocudu-dapp-package, \c ocudu-dapp-preflight,
\c ocudu-dappctl, and the Python E3 client. See OCUDU E3 management documentation.

*/
